@startuml Task Lifecycle

title Distributed Task Queue - Task Lifecycle

actor Client
participant API
participant Broker
participant "Worker Pool" as Pool
participant Registry
participant Handler
participant Repository

== Task submission (implemented) ==

Client -> API: POST /tasks
API -> API: decode + validate request
alt request invalid (malformed JSON, unknown field, or validation error)
  API --> Client: 400 { error }
else request valid
  API -> API: generate task ID (UUID), apply defaults (MaxRetries, ScheduledAt)
  API -> Repository: Create(task, status=pending)
  alt Create fails
    API --> Client: 500 { error }
  else Create succeeds
    API -> Broker: Publish(task)
    note right of Broker: Publish is non-blocking (select/default).
    note right of Broker: Returns ErrQueueFull if tasks channel is full, ctx.Err() if context already cancelled.
    alt Publish succeeds
      API --> Client: 202 { id, status: pending }
    else Publish fails
      API -> Repository: UpdateStatus(id, queue_failed)
      note right of API: Compensating update. Response always reports\nqueue_failed, whether or not this UpdateStatus call\nitself succeeds — Publish failure is the one fact\nobserved directly. If this UpdateStatus also fails,\nthe DB may still show pending; resolved later by Recovery.
      API --> Client: 202 { id, status: queue_failed }
    end
  end
end

== Async processing (implemented) ==

Pool -> Broker: Subscribe(ctx)
Broker --> Pool: out channel

loop for each task delivered via out
  Broker -> Broker: write task to pending map (happens-before send to out)
  Broker -> Pool: task

  Pool -> Registry: Get(task.Type)

  alt handler not registered
    Pool -> Pool: log error "no handler registered"
    Pool -> Repository: UpdateStatus(id, failed)
    Pool -> Broker: Ack(id)

  else handler found
    Pool -> Handler: handler(taskCtx, payload)

    alt handler succeeds
      Handler --> Pool: nil
      Pool -> Repository: UpdateStatus(id, done)
      Pool -> Broker: Ack(id)

    else handler returns error
      Handler --> Pool: error
      Pool -> Broker: Nack(id)

      alt Nack itself fails (ctx cancelled or taskID not found)
        Broker --> Pool: err != nil
        Pool -> Pool: log error, return (no Repository call)

      else retries exhausted (failed = true)
        Broker --> Pool: failed=true, err=nil
        Broker -> Broker: delete from pending
        Pool -> Repository: UpdateStatus(id, failed)

      else retry scheduled (failed = false)
        Broker --> Pool: failed=false, err=nil
        Broker -> Broker: RetryCount++, requeue into tasks channel
        note over Pool: No Repository call - status stays as-is until the task is processed again.
      end
    end
  end
end

== Status lookup (implemented) ==

Client -> API: GET /tasks/{id}
alt id is empty
  API --> Client: 400 { error }
else id provided
  API -> Repository: GetByID(id)
  alt task not found
    Repository --> API: ErrNotFound
    API --> Client: 404 { error: "task not found" }
  else other repository error
    Repository --> API: err
    API --> Client: 500 { error: "failed to get task" }
  else task found
    Repository --> API: task
    API --> Client: 200 { task }
  end
end

@enduml
